---
source: crates/broza-cli/tests/help_snapshots.rs
expression: help_for(args)
---
Execute the cleanup. Dry run by default

Usage: broza clean [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --apply
          Required to modify the disk. Without it, only simulates

      --category <ID>
          Categories to clean. Repeatable or comma-separated. Mandatory unless --risk is used

      --risk <LEVEL>
          Clean everything at this risk level or lower

          Possible values:
          - green: Safe to reclaim
          - amber: Review before reclaiming
          - red:   Information only; Broza never deletes these

      --purge
          Irreversible deletion, bypassing quarantine. Requires typing PURGE

  -y, --yes
          Assume "yes" on confirmations. Never allowed together with --purge

      --max-size <SIZE>
          Safety cap: abort if more than this amount would be removed

      --exclude <GLOB>
          Glob patterns to exclude. Repeatable; merged with `exclude` from the configuration

      --unused-after <DURATION>
          Threshold for unused-apps [default: the `unused-after` key, 1y]

      --json
          JSON output on stdout. Disables color, progress and interactivity

      --csv
          Flat CSV output on stdout. Only on tabular commands

  -o, --output <FILE>
          Write output to a file instead of stdout

      --no-color
          Disable ANSI color. Automatic without a TTY or with `NO_COLOR` set

  -q, --quiet
          Errors only. Silences progress and non-critical warnings

  -v, --verbose...
          More diagnostic detail on stderr. Repeatable

      --config <FILE>
          Alternative configuration file [default: ~/.config/broza/config.toml]

      --profile <NAME>
          Configuration profile to apply

      --no-cache
          Ignore the scan cache and force a full analysis

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
